Project: OpenEXR: OpenEXRCore (the C library) and the libdeflate it ships
URL: https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/openexr
Version: 3.5.5 (libdeflate 1.26, OpenEXR's external/deflate)
License: BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE.md; PATENTS: DreamWorks' patent grant for DWA);
         libdeflate: MIT (external/deflate/COPYING)
Used for: OpenEXR decoding in kit/intern/image (format_exr.c). Blender's imbuf reads EXR
          through the same project's C++ library (imbuf/intern/openexr/openexr_api.cpp).

Copied unmodified: src/lib/OpenEXRCore (every .c and .h but internal_zstd*.c and
internal_ht*.cpp; internal_ht_quality.h stays, base.c includes it) and external/deflate (lib/,
libdeflate.h, common_defs.h, COPYING), which compression.c includes by relative path. Every
compression decodes but zstd (it needs the vendored zstd) and HTJ2K (it needs OpenJPH, C++).
Imath is not needed: OpenEXRCore's own half conversion is used.

BUI files (bui/):
  OpenEXRConfig.h, OpenEXRConfigInternal.h, IlmThreadConfig.h, Imath/ImathConfig.h
                configuration (CMake generates these upstream)
  exr_bui.c     zstd and HTJ2K entry points, failing with EXR_ERR_FEATURE_NOT_IMPLEMENTED
